  (22, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 4 de 7 — Texto con espacios (nivel básico)</div><div class=''cloze-passage''>Last weekend, my brother and I went ___(1)___ our grandmother''s house in the countryside. We arrived ___(2)___ ten in the morning and helped her ___(3)___ the garden. She showed us how ___(4)___ plant tomatoes and beans. At noon, we had lunch together and talked about ___(5)___ childhood memories. In the afternoon, my brother played football with ___(6)___ friends from the village while I read a book ___(7)___ the porch. Before we left, our grandmother gave each of us a small basket <mark>___(8)___</mark> fresh vegetables.</div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>Elige la opción correcta para el espacio (8).</strong></p>'),
  (23, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 5 de 7 — Lectura literal</div><div class=''reading-passage''><p>Camila Torres was born in a small town in Colombia in 2001. When she was ten years old, she moved with her family to Bogotá so her parents could find better jobs. At school, Camila always loved mathematics and often stayed after class to solve extra problems with her teacher. In 2019, she won first place in a national mathematics competition for high school students. After finishing school, she received a scholarship to study engineering at a public university. Today, Camila works as a volunteer teacher on weekends, helping children in her old neighborhood learn math for free.</p></div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>Where was Camila Torres born?</strong></p>'),
  (24, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 5 de 7 — Lectura literal</div><div class=''reading-passage''><p>Camila Torres was born in a small town in Colombia in 2001. When she was ten years old, she moved with her family to Bogotá so her parents could find better jobs. At school, Camila always loved mathematics and often stayed after class to solve extra problems with her teacher. In 2019, she won first place in a national mathematics competition for high school students. After finishing school, she received a scholarship to study engineering at a public university. Today, Camila works as a volunteer teacher on weekends, helping children in her old neighborhood learn math for free.</p></div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>How old was Camila when she moved to Bogotá?</strong></p>'),
  (25, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 5 de 7 — Lectura literal</div><div class=''reading-passage''><p>Camila Torres was born in a small town in Colombia in 2001. When she was ten years old, she moved with her family to Bogotá so her parents could find better jobs. At school, Camila always loved mathematics and often stayed after class to solve extra problems with her teacher. In 2019, she won first place in a national mathematics competition for high school students. After finishing school, she received a scholarship to study engineering at a public university. Today, Camila works as a volunteer teacher on weekends, helping children in her old neighborhood learn math for free.</p></div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>Why did Camila''s family move to Bogotá?</strong></p>'),
  (26, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 5 de 7 — Lectura literal</div><div class=''reading-passage''><p>Camila Torres was born in a small town in Colombia in 2001. When she was ten years old, she moved with her family to Bogotá so her parents could find better jobs. At school, Camila always loved mathematics and often stayed after class to solve extra problems with her teacher. In 2019, she won first place in a national mathematics competition for high school students. After finishing school, she received a scholarship to study engineering at a public university. Today, Camila works as a volunteer teacher on weekends, helping children in her old neighborhood learn math for free.</p></div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>What subject did Camila love at school?</strong></p>'),
  (27, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 5 de 7 — Lectura literal</div><div class=''reading-passage''><p>Camila Torres was born in a small town in Colombia in 2001. When she was ten years old, she moved with her family to Bogotá so her parents could find better jobs. At school, Camila always loved mathematics and often stayed after class to solve extra problems with her teacher. In 2019, she won first place in a national mathematics competition for high school students. After finishing school, she received a scholarship to study engineering at a public university. Today, Camila works as a volunteer teacher on weekends, helping children in her old neighborhood learn math for free.</p></div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>What did Camila win in 2019?</strong></p>'),
  (28, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 5 de 7 — Lectura literal</div><div class=''reading-passage''><p>Camila Torres was born in a small town in Colombia in 2001. When she was ten years old, she moved with her family to Bogotá so her parents could find better jobs. At school, Camila always loved mathematics and often stayed after class to solve extra problems with her teacher. In 2019, she won first place in a national mathematics competition for high school students. After finishing school, she received a scholarship to study engineering at a public university. Today, Camila works as a volunteer teacher on weekends, helping children in her old neighborhood learn math for free.</p></div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>What did Camila study after finishing school?</strong></p>'),
  (29, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 5 de 7 — Lectura literal</div><div class=''reading-passage''><p>Camila Torres was born in a small town in Colombia in 2001. When she was ten years old, she moved with her family to Bogotá so her parents could find better jobs. At school, Camila always loved mathematics and often stayed after class to solve extra problems with her teacher. In 2019, she won first place in a national mathematics competition for high school students. After finishing school, she received a scholarship to study engineering at a public university. Today, Camila works as a volunteer teacher on weekends, helping children in her old neighborhood learn math for free.</p></div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>What does Camila do today on weekends?</strong></p>'),
  (30, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 6 de 7 — Lectura inferencial</div><div class=''reading-passage''><p>For millions of people around the world, having a pet is much more than a hobby. Dogs, cats, and even smaller animals like rabbits or birds become part of the family almost immediately. Many pet owners say that coming home to a wagging tail or a soft purring sound helps them forget a stressful day at work. Scientists have also found that spending time with animals can lower stress hormones and even improve heart health. Still, taking care of a pet is a serious commitment: it requires time, money, and patience, especially during the first few months. Despite the extra responsibility, most owners agree that the emotional connection they build with their pet makes every challenge worth it.</p></div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>What is the writer mainly trying to do in this text?</strong></p>'),
  (31, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 6 de 7 — Lectura inferencial</div><div class=''reading-passage''><p>For millions of people around the world, having a pet is much more than a hobby. Dogs, cats, and even smaller animals like rabbits or birds become part of the family almost immediately. Many pet owners say that coming home to a wagging tail or a soft purring sound helps them forget a stressful day at work. Scientists have also found that spending time with animals can lower stress hormones and even improve heart health. Still, taking care of a pet is a serious commitment: it requires time, money, and patience, especially during the first few months. Despite the extra responsibility, most owners agree that the emotional connection they build with their pet makes every challenge worth it.</p></div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>What can be inferred about pet owners'' first few months with a new pet?</strong></p>'),
  (32, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 6 de 7 — Lectura inferencial</div><div class=''reading-passage''><p>For millions of people around the world, having a pet is much more than a hobby. Dogs, cats, and even smaller animals like rabbits or birds become part of the family almost immediately. Many pet owners say that coming home to a wagging tail or a soft purring sound helps them forget a stressful day at work. Scientists have also found that spending time with animals can lower stress hormones and even improve heart health. Still, taking care of a pet is a serious commitment: it requires time, money, and patience, especially during the first few months. Despite the extra responsibility, most owners agree that the emotional connection they build with their pet makes every challenge worth it.</p></div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>According to the text, what does the writer suggest about the relationship between people and pets?</strong></p>'),
  (33, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 6 de 7 — Lectura inferencial</div><div class=''reading-passage''><p>For millions of people around the world, having a pet is much more than a hobby. Dogs, cats, and even smaller animals like rabbits or birds become part of the family almost immediately. Many pet owners say that coming home to a wagging tail or a soft purring sound helps them forget a stressful day at work. Scientists have also found that spending time with animals can lower stress hormones and even improve heart health. Still, taking care of a pet is a serious commitment: it requires time, money, and patience, especially during the first few months. Despite the extra responsibility, most owners agree that the emotional connection they build with their pet makes every challenge worth it.</p></div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>What tone does the writer use when discussing the responsibilities of owning a pet?</strong></p>'),
  (34, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 6 de 7 — Lectura inferencial</div><div class=''reading-passage''><p>For millions of people around the world, having a pet is much more than a hobby. Dogs, cats, and even smaller animals like rabbits or birds become part of the family almost immediately. Many pet owners say that coming home to a wagging tail or a soft purring sound helps them forget a stressful day at work. Scientists have also found that spending time with animals can lower stress hormones and even improve heart health. Still, taking care of a pet is a serious commitment: it requires time, money, and patience, especially during the first few months. Despite the extra responsibility, most owners agree that the emotional connection they build with their pet makes every challenge worth it.</p></div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>Why does the writer likely mention scientific findings about stress hormones?</strong></p>'),
  (35, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 7 de 7 — Texto con espacios (nivel avanzado)</div><div class=''cloze-passage''>In recent years, renewable energy sources such as solar and wind power <mark>___(1)___</mark> become more affordable than ever before. ___(2)___ fossil fuels still dominate global energy production, many countries are investing heavily in clean alternatives. Governments ___(3)___ introduced new policies to encourage citizens and businesses to reduce their carbon footprint. ___(4)___, some industries continue to resist these changes because of the high initial costs. ___(5)___ these obstacles, experts believe that renewable energy will eventually replace most fossil fuels. Critics argue, ___(6)___, that the transition should happen faster to prevent further damage to the environment. Communities ___(7)___ already begun to notice the benefits of cleaner air in cities that have adopted electric transportation. ___(8)___ progress has been made, there is still a long way to go before renewable energy becomes the main source of power worldwide. ___(9)___ the challenges, younger generations remain optimistic about a cleaner future. ___(10)___ these efforts continue, the planet could see significant improvements within the next few decades.</div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>Elige la opción correcta para el espacio (1).</strong></p>'),
  (36, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 7 de 7 — Texto con espacios (nivel avanzado)</div><div class=''cloze-passage''>In recent years, renewable energy sources such as solar and wind power ___(1)___ become more affordable than ever before. <mark>___(2)___</mark> fossil fuels still dominate global energy production, many countries are investing heavily in clean alternatives. Governments ___(3)___ introduced new policies to encourage citizens and businesses to reduce their carbon footprint. ___(4)___, some industries continue to resist these changes because of the high initial costs. ___(5)___ these obstacles, experts believe that renewable energy will eventually replace most fossil fuels. Critics argue, ___(6)___, that the transition should happen faster to prevent further damage to the environment. Communities ___(7)___ already begun to notice the benefits of cleaner air in cities that have adopted electric transportation. ___(8)___ progress has been made, there is still a long way to go before renewable energy becomes the main source of power worldwide. ___(9)___ the challenges, younger generations remain optimistic about a cleaner future. ___(10)___ these efforts continue, the planet could see significant improvements within the next few decades.</div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>Elige la opción correcta para el espacio (2).</strong></p>'),
