  (38, '<div class=''sim-part-tag''>Parte 7 de 7 — Texto con espacios (nivel avanzado)</div><div class=''cloze-passage''>In recent years, renewable energy sources such as solar and wind power ___(1)___ become more affordable than ever before. ___(2)___ fossil fuels still dominate global energy production, many countries are investing heavily in clean alternatives. Governments ___(3)___ introduced new policies to encourage citizens and businesses to reduce their carbon footprint. <mark>___(4)___</mark>, some industries continue to resist these changes because of the high initial costs. ___(5)___ these obstacles, experts believe that renewable energy will eventually replace most fossil fuels. Critics argue, ___(6)___, that the transition should happen faster to prevent further damage to the environment. Communities ___(7)___ already begun to notice the benefits of cleaner air in cities that have adopted electric transportation. ___(8)___ progress has been made, there is still a long way to go before renewable energy becomes the main source of power worldwide. ___(9)___ the challenges, younger generations remain optimistic about a cleaner future. ___(10)___ these efforts continue, the planet could see significant improvements within the next few decades.</div><p style=''margin-top:8px;''><strong>Elige la opción correcta para el espacio (4).</strong></p>'),
